# The projects built with this workshop are cloned into their own directories,
# beside this one and never inside it. This file is the second lock on that
# door: if a clone lands in here anyway, git will not stage it.
#
# One line per registered project, using the same id as projects/registry.json.
# Registering a project adds its id here too.
#
# Why this matters: a project cloned inside this directory is staged by a plain
# `git add -A` as an embedded repository — a pointer to a commit that nobody
# who clones Bottega can fetch — and the workshop then carries a broken link to
# the application. Observed on 14 September 2026: nested and unignored, the
# clone staged as mode 160000 with git's embedded-repository warning; with the
# id listed here, the same command staged nothing.

/zibaldone/
